name: sim.unpackUInt8Table
description: Unpacks a string (or part of it) into an array of uint8 numbers
luaSynopsis: list uint8Numbers = sim.unpackUInt8Table(bytes data, int startUint8Index = 0, int uint8Count = 0)
pythonSynopsis: int[] uint8Numbers = sim.unpackUInt8Table(buffer data, int startUint8Index = 0, int uint8Count = 0)
inputs:
1. data: string (values between 0 and 255) that contains uint8 numbers
2. startUint8Index: zero-based index from which on data should be unpacked (from data[startUint8Index]). Can be omitted in which case 0 is used.
3. uint8Count: amount of uint8s that should be unpacked. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum of uint8s should be unpacked from the indicated startUint8Index).
outputs:
1. uint8Numbers: array containing uint8 numbers
replacedBy:
- name: unpackArray, class: app, file: app_unpackArray.method
